      <slug></slug>
      <title>Release management in Debian - can we do better?</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Debian</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Using some practical examples, mostly from personal experience,&#x9;of things that have not been handled optimaly during the lenny release cycle, I will give my view on how they could have been handled better. I will also take a more general look at the current role of release managers and the release team in Debian and look back on the Etch-and-a-half release.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="621">Frans Pop</person>
      </persons>
